# The guild mage: one per friendly settlement, at the circle in the stamped
# mage guild. Sells translocation (Window_TSC_Translocate) and enchantment
# (Window_TSC_Enchant), both for silver.

dialogue TSC_Dialogue_TownMage

== start ==
The mage is sitting on the edge of an inlaid marble circle, eating an apple, and does not stand up when you come in.

"Two things for sale, and neither of them is advice. I can move you, and I can enchant your gear. Both cost silver, and the silver is not the hard part."

* "Move us how far?" -> travel
* "Enchant our gear?" -> enchant
* "Neither today." -> end

== travel ==
"As far as there's a circle at the other end, which means any town that isn't trying to kill us this season." He turns the apple over. "Everyone standing in the ring goes: your people, your beasts, whatever they're carrying. What's lying on the floor stays on the floor, and I won't hear a word about it afterward."

* "Show me the circles." -> end
    do mage_translocate()
* "Not yet." -> end

== enchant ==
"Given time and silver, your weapons and armor be taught something extra: a ward, a lightness, a bite, a quickness." He finishes the apple. "Plain armor and weapons only. One to a piece."

* "Show me the bench." -> end
    do mage_enchant()
* "Another time." -> end
